Track 2: Vance’s Siding, 03:00
- Story & Context: Tucked behind the diesel-soaked weeds of Vance's Siding, disgraced line-mechanic Sela spliced bootleg cassette loops on a battery-operated four-track while an unhoused assembly droid quietly rocked a blind sensor unit in the bed of an open gondola car. The bitter tang of burning resin drifted into the cold night as Sela layered pitch-bent synth chords over drop-tuned guitar chugs, confessing into a bruised microphone about the midnight shift she rewrote factory routines to spare the unfinished units. When the yardmaster's searchlights swept the gravel, the droid did not move, using its physical frame to shield the slumbering chassis while the steel drum rung out like a chapel chime. Sela leaned into the wind and muttered the track's cyclical confession: "I stole your clock-cycle so you could finally sleep."
