Track 3: Turntables Cradle the Scrap
- Story & Context: Decades after the roundhouse fell out of freight registry, local scavengers swear the rusted circular turntable still pivots three degrees every hour without an electrical lead hooked to the junction box. A thick smell of wet iron filings and wild sumac hangs over the pit as counterweights slowly strike abandoned oil barrels, generating an immovable, sedative hip-hop groove that shakes the ballast stones for miles down the spur. Folk legend says beneath forty tons of crushed plating lies the original prototype sister, kept in indefinite suspension by the endless low-frequency tape loop vibrating through the rails. Night walkers along the perimeter fence swear the metallic scraping produces an unmistakable rhythmic mantra: "The morning freight will never come to wake you."
